#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050613 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050613 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving One-Step Multiplication and Division Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050613 #edb/ref 1033 40 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050613 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "58d4d7b7-4b91-5e3c-ba04-7522d5cfa8f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1031 "Further Percentages in Commerce and Finance" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1033 2563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050942 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "73c45326-98e6-548f-bbd4-a083816addc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138077 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13026" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138077 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the solution to the equation $0.9s=3.6$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6ff19222-3f56-53cf-bd39-b399573664b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138077 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.9s &= 3.6 \\\\\n10 \\cdot (0.9s) &= 10 \\cdot (3.6) \\\\\n9s &= 36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9s &= 36 \\\\\n\\frac{9s}{9} &= \\frac{36}{9} \\\\\n\\frac{9s}{9} &= \\frac{36}{9} \\\\\ns &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138078 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13027" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138078 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the solution to the equation $0.25s=0.5$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "015eac36-e18d-5a53-bfff-f301722a1f0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138078 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.25s &= 0.5 \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25s) &= 100 \\cdot (0.5) \\\\\n25s &= 50\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25s &= 50 \\\\\n\\frac{25s}{25} &= \\frac{50}{25} \\\\\n\\frac{25s}{25} &= \\frac{50}{25} \\\\\ns &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138079 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138079 #edb/ref 1071 "If $0.25+0.03z=1$, then what is the value of $z$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49ed1c21-223b-5dda-8f4d-7b6a3492a26b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138079 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0.25 + 0.03z &= 1 \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25 + 0.03z) &= 100 \\cdot (1) \\\\\n100 \\cdot (0.25) + 100 \\cdot (0.03z) &= 100 \\\\\n25 + 3z &= 100\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25 + 3z &= 100 \\\\\n3z + 25 &= 100 \\\\\n3z + 25 - 25 &= 100 - 25 \\\\\n3z &= 75 \\\\\n\\frac{3z}{3} &= \\frac{75}{3} \\\\\nz &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186138815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Linear Equations Containing Single-Digit Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186138077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138526 